# No rules on purpose, and worth reading before any are added back.
#
# It used to carry `*.kicad_pcb -text` and `*.kicad_dru -text` for the Glow
# faceplate, whose board file had its SHA-256 pinned in an asset guard. Both the
# faceplate and the guard were deleted on 2026-08-14 with the flow layer, and no
# tracked KiCad file is left, so the rules have no subject and are removed rather
# than left pointing at nothing.
#
# The trap they existed for is not gone, and the M6 hardware faceplate will meet
# it: `git config core.autocrlf` is `true` on the development machine, and a
# KiCad board is text, so a fresh clone or a new worktree receives CRLF while the
# committed blob is LF. Any hash pinned over such a file then fails on a tree
# that is in fact correct. If a board file is ever pinned again, restore the
# `-text` rule for its extension in the same commit.
#
# The other pinned artefacts needed no entry: a KiCad preview PNG is detected as
# binary and left alone, and the official DXF was local-only under .reference/.

# 2026-08-30: the subject is back, and the rule with it. hardware/lib/DaisyKiCad
# is vendored third-party and pinned by sha256 in its own checksums.sha256, so
# every KiCad text format has to round-trip byte-identically through a clone.
# Without these lines the first fresh clone on this machine turns LF into CRLF
# and the checksums fail on a tree that is correct. Proven, not assumed: a clone
# into a temporary directory reproduces the committed sums.
*.kicad_sym  -text
*.kicad_mod  -text
*.kicad_pcb  -text
*.kicad_sch  -text
*.kicad_pro  -text
*.kicad_dru  -text

# Extensions are not enough on their own: the first clone check passed the three
# KiCad files above and still failed on LICENSE, which has no extension and so
# matched no rule. What is pinned here is a whole vendored directory, so the
# attribute belongs to the directory.
hardware/lib/**  -text

# 2026-10-02 (P4-3 spec §4.5): build.py writes these five files with LF. With
# core.autocrlf=true a checkout writes CRLF, the index keeps the CRLF size, and
# every build.py run then leaves them "modified" with an empty diff. eol=lf
# makes the checkout write LF too, so build.py should leave status empty.
# Observed: after this change, build.py left `git status` clean in the P4-3
# worktree. Not reproduced: the "modified" state itself did not appear in that
# worktree before the change, so the trap and the fix were not seen side by side.
hardware/reva/bom-*.csv          text eol=lf
hardware/reva/review.md          text eol=lf
hardware/reva/kicad/*-lib-table  text eol=lf
